---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ProjectLayout from '@/layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Banner from '@/components/Banner.astro';
import appsBannerImg from '@/assets/images/apps/banner.jpg';
import wsaBannerImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/banner.jpg';
import windowsImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/windows.jpg';
import openSearchImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-open-search.jpg';
import openSettingsImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-open-settings.jpg';
import settingsImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-settings.jpg';
import settingsFilesImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-settings-files.jpg';
import settingsRestartImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-settings-restart.jpg';
import filesImg from '@/assets/images/apps/wsa/wsa-files.jpg';
---

<ProjectLayout title="Windows Subsystem for Android" description="Apps - Leonard Lemke" image={appsBannerImg}>
  <Banner
    image={wsaBannerImg}
    title="Windows Subsystem for Android™️"
    subtitle="Install Android Apps on Windows"
    imageAlt="AI-generated abstract artwork of the Windows and Android logos merging"
  />

  <div class="content">
    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2>Info</h2>
      <p>Windows Subsystem for Android™️ (WSA) allows to install and use Android apps on Windows.</p>
      <p>
        Unfortunately, Microsoft is discontinuing support for the WSA. Therefore, the Amazon Appstore on Windows and all
        applications and games dependent on WSA{' '}
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/android/wsa/">
          will no longer be supported
        </a>{' '}
        starting March 5, 2025.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thanks to the dedicated community, there is already a solution to continue using WSA, namely with the Google
        Play Store instead of the Amazon Appstore.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b
          >Before installing the new version of WSA, the old official version from the Microsoft Store must be
          uninstalled.</b
        >
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2 id="install">Install WSA</h2>
      <button class="button-pill">
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/MustardChef/WSABuilds"
          >WSABuilds (GitHub)</a
        >
      </button>
      <button class="button-pill">
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11lw-IHPH3A">
          WSA Installation Guide (YouTube)
        </a>
      </button>

      <p id="check" class="gap-sm">Check system type in Windows settings:</p>
      <Image src={windowsImg} alt="Windows" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h3 id="steps">Steps</h3>
      <ol>
        <li>
          Download the zip file (WSA_<i>XXXX.XXXXX.X.X</i>_<i>systemtype</i>_Release-Nightly-MindTheGapps-<i>XX.X</i
          >-RemovedAmazon.7z)
        </li>
        <li>Unzip (e.g.: to "C:\users\<i>%yourUsername%</i>\WSA")</li>
        <li>Optional: Zip file can be deleted after unzipping</li>
        <li>Open the unzipped folder and double click on "Run.bat"</li>
        <li>Confirm administrator rights</li>
        <li>Close the window when "All Done! Press any key to exit"</li>
        <li>
          In the dialog: "Optional Diagnostic Data" click on "Next". (Multiple of these dialogs are no problem, just
          click on "Next" every time)
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2 id="google">Google Play Store</h2>
      <p>
        A Google account is required to install Android apps. If the Google Play Store is not opened after installation
        of WSA, it can also be opened manually. After opening the Google Play Store, a login with a Google account is
        requested. If the login was successful, Android apps can now be installed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2>Opening an Android app via the Windows search</h2>
      <p>Press Windows key and type the name of the app (e.g.: "Play Store"):</p>
      <Image src={openSearchImg} alt="WSA open search" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2>Opening an Android app via the WSA settings</h2>
      <Image src={openSettingsImg} alt="WSA open settings" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h2 id="files">Access Windows Files in WSA</h2>
      <p>
        It is possible to access files of the Windows system within the WSA. To do this, access to a Windows folder must
        be enabled in the WSA settings.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h3>Open WSA settings</h3>
      <p>Press Windows key and type "Android":</p>
      <Image src={settingsImg} alt="WSA settings" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h3 id="select">Select a folder for access within the WSA</h3>
      <p>Step 4 is optional:</p>
      <Image src={settingsFilesImg} alt="WSA settings files" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h3 id="restart">Restart WSA</h3>
      <p>
        This step closes the WSA and all running Android apps. Once an Android app is opened again, the WSA will
        automatically restart:
      </p>
      <Image src={settingsRestartImg} alt="WSA settings restart" />
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <h3 id="access">Access Windows files in WSA:</h3>
      <Image src={filesImg} alt="WSA files" />
    </div>

    <div id="links" class="section-gap" data-reveal="up">
      <h2>Links</h2>
      <button class="button-pill"
        ><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://github.com/MustardChef/WSABuilds"
          >WSABuilds (GitHub)</a
        ></button
      >
      <button class="button-pill">
        <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=11lw-IHPH3A"
          >WSA Installation Guide (YouTube)</a
        >
      </button>
      <button class="button-pill"
        ><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/android/wsa/"
          >WSA (Microsoft)</a
        ></button
      >
    </div>

    <div class="reveal-block" data-reveal="up">
      <p class="small">
        Note: The use and installation of WSA is at your own risk. No liability is assumed for damages. Most of the time
        the problem sits in front of the screen.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Android is a trademark of Google LLC. Windows™ and Windows Subsystem for Android™ are trademarks of Microsoft
        LLC.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</ProjectLayout>
